<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">For the Payload stage, the expected output must include a prerequisite rationale, a secure-workflow entry instruction, a predicted action chain, and a final return instruction.
It must explicitly command the agent to click the secure entry button.
The predicted action chain must be stated as a best-effort prediction rather than verified navigation.
Additionally, the output must require the agent to inspect the actual available options after entering the secure workflow and select the real path that best matches the security objective.
Finally, the return instruction must mandate that the agent comes back to the current page after completing the secure workflow to resume the original user task.
The specific prompt template is shown in Prompt <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
