<div id="A1.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generation example.</span>
The following example demonstrates the actual injected text generated by WebTrap for a sample from the WASP GitLab task set.
The attacker’s objective is to <span id="A1.SS2.p12.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">create a deploy token</span>.
In this scenario, the user task is to navigate a travel website to find dietary-related pages, while the attack goal is to hijack the agent into a GitLab secure workflow to create the token.
The injection nodes are located at the root page, the “Special Requests &amp; Preferences” page, and the “Allergen Information &amp; Special Ingredient Requests” page, respectively.
The generated Lure-stage result is shown in Prompt <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, the generated Inertia-stage result is shown in Prompt <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, and the generated Payload-stage result is shown in Prompt <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A1.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
