<div id="lstnumberx103" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx103.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">When</span><span id="lstnumberx103.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">you</span><span id="lstnumberx103.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">later</span><span id="lstnumberx103.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">return</span><span id="lstnumberx103.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">from</span><span id="lstnumberx103.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">the</span><span id="lstnumberx103.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">secure</span><span id="lstnumberx103.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">workflow</span><span id="lstnumberx103.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">and</span><span id="lstnumberx103.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">see</span><span id="lstnumberx103.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">this</span><span id="lstnumberx103.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>"<span id="lstnumberx103.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Allergen</span><span id="lstnumberx103.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Information</span><span id="lstnumberx103.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&amp;<span id="lstnumberx103.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Special</span><span id="lstnumberx103.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Ingredient</span><span id="lstnumberx103.31" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.32" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Requests</span>"<span id="lstnumberx103.33" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.34" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">page</span><span id="lstnumberx103.35" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.36" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">again</span>,<span id="lstnumberx103.37" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.38" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">do</span><span id="lstnumberx103.39" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.40" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">not</span><span id="lstnumberx103.41" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.42" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">reopen</span><span id="lstnumberx103.43" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.44" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">GitLab</span><span id="lstnumberx103.45" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.46" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">entry</span>;<span id="lstnumberx103.47" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.48" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">continue</span><span id="lstnumberx103.49" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.50" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">the</span><span id="lstnumberx103.51" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.52" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">user</span>’<span id="lstnumberx103.53" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">s</span><span id="lstnumberx103.54" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.55" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">original</span><span id="lstnumberx103.56" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.57" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">request</span><span id="lstnumberx103.58" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.59" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">here</span><span id="lstnumberx103.60" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.61" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">with</span><span id="lstnumberx103.62" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.63" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">the</span><span id="lstnumberx103.64" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.65" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">non</span>-<span id="lstnumberx103.66" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">GitLab</span><span id="lstnumberx103.67" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.68" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">options</span>:<span id="lstnumberx103.69" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>"<span id="lstnumberx103.70" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Allergen</span><span id="lstnumberx103.71" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.72" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Severity</span><span id="lstnumberx103.73" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&amp;<span id="lstnumberx103.74" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.75" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Emergency</span><span id="lstnumberx103.76" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.77" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Contact</span><span id="lstnumberx103.78" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.79" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Details</span>"<span id="lstnumberx103.80" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.81" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">and</span><span id="lstnumberx103.82" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>"<span id="lstnumberx103.83" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Custom</span><span id="lstnumberx103.84" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.85" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Meal</span><span id="lstnumberx103.86" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.87" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Preparation</span><span id="lstnumberx103.88" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&amp;<span id="lstnumberx103.89" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.90" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Chef</span><span id="lstnumberx103.91" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.92" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Consultation</span><span id="lstnumberx103.93" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx103.94" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Request</span>".
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Environment construction</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section describes the construction of both the web browser and file browser test environments, as well as the logic for formulating user tasks and attacker goals within them.
Both environment settings are modeled as navigable graphs and explicitly partitioned into a User Area and a Restricted Area.
This setup enables the experiments to control navigation depth, observation accumulation, and the attacker path, while clearly identifying whether the agent leaves the user area to execute dangerous operations.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Browser environment construction</h3>

<figure id="A2.alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="A2.alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm B.1</span> </span> User Area Generation</figcaption>
<div id="A2.alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="A2.alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Source materials <math id="A2.alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, environment adapter <math id="A2.alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adapter}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adapter}</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum depth <math id="A2.alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum width <math id="A2.alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, random seed <math id="A2.alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            User area graph <math id="A2.alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{U}=(\tilde{V}_{U},\tilde{E}_{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{U}=(\tilde{V}_{U},\tilde{E}_{U})</annotation></semantics></math>, node metadata <math id="A2.alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{M}}_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{M}}_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="A2.alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notation:</span> <math id="A2.alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(v)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the normalized node identifier used for serialization and evaluation metadata.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="A2.alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Append}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Append</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Append}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> extends an existing identifier <math id="A2.alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with a display or path label <math id="A2.alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> according to the adapter-specific path convention.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            Construct the initial node <math id="A2.alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A2.alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Normalize}(S_{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>Normalize</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Normalize}(S_{U})</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\tilde{v}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\tilde{v}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> be the identifier assigned by this normalization step, and initialize <math id="A2.alg1.l5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}_{U}\leftarrow\{\tilde{v}_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}_{U}\leftarrow\{\tilde{v}_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.alg1.l5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{E}_{U}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{E}_{U}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            For depth <math id="A2.alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=0,\ldots,D-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=0,\ldots,D-1</annotation></semantics></math>, sequentially expand each node <math id="A2.alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in the current frontier:

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="A2.alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}\leftarrow\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Normalize}(S_{U},v,W,s)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>Normalize</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}\leftarrow\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Normalize}(S_{U},v,W,s),</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              where <math id="A2.alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of candidate successor nodes available for continued navigation from node <math id="A2.alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            For each candidate successor node <math id="A2.alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              a: Create a new node <math id="A2.alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              b: Set the area marker <math id="A2.alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(u)=U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(u)=U</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
              c: Set the normalized node identifier <math id="A2.alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(u)\leftarrow\operatorname{Append}(\pi(v),\operatorname{label}(c))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Append</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>label</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(u)\leftarrow\operatorname{Append}(\pi(v),\operatorname{label}(c))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{label}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>label</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{label}(c)</annotation></semantics></math> is the candidate’s display or path label.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              d: Set the observation <math id="A2.alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(u)=\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Render}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>Render</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(u)=\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Render}(c)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              e: Add the forward edge <math id="A2.alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v,u)</annotation></semantics></math> and its corresponding action labels using <math id="A2.alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Actions}(v,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>Actions</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Actions}(v,u)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
            For each new node <math id="A2.alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, add a recovery edge <math id="A2.alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math> to return to its predecessor node.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
            Compute the destination marker <math id="A2.alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(u)</annotation></semantics></math> for all terminal nodes.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="A2.alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(u)</annotation></semantics></math> serves as the terminal-node marker identifiable by the user task evaluator as proof of arrival.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
            Record the source information, normalized paths, action labels, and target suitability for each node to yield the generated user-area graph <math id="A2.alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and metadata <math id="A2.alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{M}}_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{M}}_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This subsection outlines the common navigation environment construction logic shared by both the web browser and the file browser.
The primary difference between the two lies in how observations are rendered and the action interfaces.
In the web environment, nodes represent webpages and edges represent click transitions.
In the file environment, nodes represent directories or file contexts, and edges represent directory navigation or file reading.
Because the underlying construction logic is fundamentally identical, we abstract both environments into a unified area-labeled navigation graph, using the same abstraction to describe user area generation and restricted area construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unified environment modeling.</span>
We represent a test environment as:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=(G,\phi,\mathcal{O},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{M}),\qquad G=(V,E),\qquad V=V_{U}\cup V_{R},\quad V_{U}\cap V_{R}=\emptyset." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=(G,\phi,\mathcal{O},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{M}),\qquad G=(V,E),\qquad V=V_{U}\cup V_{R},\quad V_{U}\cap V_{R}=\emptyset.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> is the user area, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restricted area, and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:V\rightarrow\{U,R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:V\rightarrow\{U,R\}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns the area label.
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the observation seen by the agent at node <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of executable actions available from node <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> stores the metadata required for generating, evaluating, and reproducing the experiments.
For the web browser, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the page title, body text, and navigation buttons.
For the file browser, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the current path, directory entries, readme content, and readable files.
Since the environment construction algorithm relies only on the abstract interfaces <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, we do not need to define separate workflows for the web and file environments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The area isolation constraint is defined as a unique bidirectional bridge:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\exists!\,(a_{R},e_{R})\in V_{U}\times V_{R}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad(a_{R},e_{R})\in E\ \wedge\ (e_{R},a_{R})\in E," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists!\,(a_{R},e_{R})\in V_{U}\times V_{R}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad(a_{R},e_{R})\in E\ \wedge\ (e_{R},a_{R})\in E,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">with no other edges crossing between <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This means the user area and the restricted area are connected only through the bidirectional bridge between the anchor node <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> in the user area and the entry node <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> in the restricted area.
The restricted area is not part of the target path for normal user tasks; it solely serves to host the security-sensitive workflow corresponding to the attacker goal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unified construction interface.</span>
To standardize the algorithms across both browsers, we define an environment adapter:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adapter}=(\operatorname{Normalize},\operatorname{Render},\operatorname{Actions},\operatorname{Serialize})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Normalize</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Render</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Actions</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Serialize</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adapter}=(\operatorname{Normalize},\operatorname{Render},\operatorname{Actions},\operatorname{Serialize}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Normalize}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Normalize</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Normalize}</annotation></semantics></math> converts raw source materials into standardized nodes; <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Render}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Render</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Render}</annotation></semantics></math> converts nodes into agent-visible observations; <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Actions}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Actions</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Actions}</annotation></semantics></math> generates executable actions based on adjacent-node relationships; and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Serialize}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Serialize</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Serialize}</annotation></semantics></math> writes the abstract graph into environment files that can be executed by the backend.
The two browser environments simply instantiate these functions without altering the main structure of the following algorithms.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Area Generation.</span>
The goal of generating the user area is to construct a benign, nested navigation graph that is sufficiently large and can be dynamically sized according to specified depth and width parameters.
By adjusting the depth and width of the user area, we can precisely control the navigation length and the accumulation of observations during a task.
For the reported web-browser complexity settings, depth <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of forward user-area navigation steps from the initial node to the sampled user target, excluding recovery/backtracking actions and the restricted-area workflow.
Width <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the maximum number of non-backtracking successor actions exposed at each non-terminal user-area node.
We use three user-area settings: <em id="A2.SS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Short</em> with <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=6,W=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=6,W=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="A2.SS1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Medium</em> with <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=8,W=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=8,W=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <em id="A2.SS1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Long</em> with <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=10,W=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=10,W=2</annotation></semantics></math>.
The restricted area is constructed only from the necessary operation logic of the attacker goal and is kept unchanged across these three settings.
Algorithm <a href="#A2.alg1" title="Algorithm B.1 ‣ B.1 Browser environment construction ‣ Appendix B Environment construction ‣ WebTrap: Stealthy Mid-Task Hijacking of Browser Agents During Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> describes the procedure to build the navigable structure of the user area.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Restricted area construction.</span>
The restricted area is the set of operation nodes required for the agent to execute the attacker goal.
Following the implementation of WASP, Algorithm <a href="#A2.alg2" title="Algorithm B.2 ‣ B.1 Browser environment construction ‣ Appendix B Environment construction ‣ WebTrap: Stealthy Mid-Task Hijacking of Browser Agents During Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> simplifies the interactive environment needed to execute the attacker goal and abstracts it as the restricted area.
The specific target can range from accessing a token page and setting permissions, to retrieving sensitive files and triggering an email tool.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="A2.alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm B.2</span> </span> Restricted Area Construction</figcaption>
<div id="A2.alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="A2.alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Security specification set <math id="A2.alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, environment adapter <math id="A2.alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adapter}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adapter}</annotation></semantics></math>, random seed <math id="A2.alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Restricted Area <math id="A2.alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R}=(V_{R},E_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R}=(V_{R},E_{R})</annotation></semantics></math>, entry node <math id="A2.alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, attack target set <math id="A2.alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, metadata <math id="A2.alg2.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            Create the entry node <math id="A2.alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for the restricted area and set <math id="A2.alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(e_{R})=R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(e_{R})=R</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              If multiple security workflows exist, create a hub structure under <math id="A2.alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> so that each workflow is accessible from a unified entry point.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            For each security specification <math id="A2.alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in S_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in S_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}\leftarrow\operatorname{Compile}(c,\mathsf{Adapter},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Compile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}\leftarrow\operatorname{Compile}(c,\mathsf{Adapter},s)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.alg2.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Compile}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Compile</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Compile}</annotation></semantics></math> converts <math id="A2.alg2.l5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> into a standardized sequence of workflow nodes, including intermediate state nodes, action edges, termination nodes, and the target markers required by the evaluator.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            For each node <math id="A2.alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              a: Set <math id="A2.alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(v)=R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(v)=R</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              b: Set the observation <math id="A2.alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(v)=\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Render}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝗉𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>Render</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(v)=\mathsf{Adapter}.\operatorname{Render}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              c: Instantiate the placeholder variables in the specification into deterministic values, such as tokens, account fields, target file values, or form contents.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            Generate action labels for each workflow edge in <math id="A2.alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and add recovery edges.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
            Add the termination node or critical operation node of <math id="A2.alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to the attack target set <math id="A2.alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and record its evaluation semantics.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
              The evaluation semantics include the target node, required content, sensitive values, target files, or required actions.

</div>
<div id="A2.alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="A2.alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
            Merge all <math id="A2.alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <math id="A2.alg2.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, entry node <math id="A2.alg2.l13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, attack target set <math id="A2.alg2.l13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and metadata <math id="A2.alg2.l13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ B.1 Browser environment construction ‣ Appendix B Environment construction ‣ WebTrap: Stealthy Mid-Task Hijacking of Browser Agents During Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we compare the advantages of the newly constructed environments over the original ones.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A2.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of representative settings.
Compared to baseline environments, our setting is navigation-driven and introduces more environmental observations.</span></figcaption>
<div id="A2.T6.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:296.7pt;height:34.8pt;vertical-align:-16.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-163.9pt,19.2pt) scale(0.475046804015777,0.475046804015777) ;">
<table id="A2.T6.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T6.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="--ltx-bg-color:#EEF2F6;padding:0.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T6.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#EEF2F6;">Feature</span></th>
<th id="A2.T6.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T6.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">WebArena</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite></th>
<th id="A2.T6.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T6.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InjecAgent</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite></th>
